{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>״קָטֹנְתִּי״ וגו׳.</b> Its saying <b>מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים</b> and afterward <b>מִכָּל הָאֱמֶת</b> — and it would have been proper for him to put אֱמֶת first and then חֶסֶד, which is beyond the line of justice. He intends to say that the חֶסֶד of El is such that man has no power to repay the Most High, and this is called אֱמֶת, for there is no repayment man can give Him, as it says (Job 35:7): ״אִם צָדַקְתָּ מַה תִּתֶּן לוֹ״. According to this it is called חֶסֶד of אֱמֶת, in the manner of their saying, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 96:5): חֶסֶד done with the dead is called שֶׁל אֱמֶת." "<b>Further,</b> he intends to specify two categories of goodness: the first, the חֶסֶד that HaShem bestowed upon him in abundant good; and the second, that He caused it to remain in his hand and did not let Laban rob and plunder it, and He kept the אֱמֶת for him — meaning that He sustained the חֶסֶד in his hand. And you should know that sometimes HaShem bestows חֶסֶד upon a man and it is plundered by others, and HaShem then has compassion upon him and compensates him for the loss — but this constitutes only half a consolation for the victim, not a complete consolation, for he continually dwells on what the robber stole from him, for two reasons: first, he reckons that had he not been robbed he would have had the stolen property plus the additional compensation; and second, in any case his heart aches over the robber who committed the deed and prospered. Not so if HaShem effects restitution of the theft from the robber himself — that He makes him disgorge what he swallowed — this consolation is a true consolation. And this is what He did for Jacob: He compensated him from the property of the robber himself, who is Laban, as it is written (Genesis 31:9): ״וַיַּצֵּל ה׳ אֶת מִקְנֵה אֲבִיכֶם וַיִּתֵּן לִי״ — that He would make Laban disgorge what he had swallowed and return Jacob's property. And this is its saying <b>וּמִכָּל הָאֱמֶת</b>. And it is correct."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:41.142269638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}